===(Initial Setup on Pi device)
1) Create a project folder

mkdir ~/PROJECT_NAME
cd ~/PROJECT_NAME

2) Create a virtual environment
This avoids the "externally managed environment" issue on Pi OS:

python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate

Terminal prompt will now show (venv) to indicate the venv is active

3) Install required Python packages

pip install pyserial python-osc

4) Create the main script file 

nano serial_to_osc.py

5) Paste the scaffold found in this folder in the nano editor

Edit > Paste

6) Run the script

python3 serial_to_osc.py

